# The SNAP image (containers/Dockerfile.snap) copies nothing from the repository
# — it only needs the Dockerfile itself. Without this file Docker still packs and
# ships the whole working tree to the daemon, .venv and .git included, for no
# benefit.
#
# Written as an allowlist so a new large directory never silently rejoins the
# context: everything is excluded, then the few paths a build may need are
# added back.
*

!containers/

# Kept available so an image that does install the package (a future application
# image, or a local build for reproducing a CI run) has the sources it needs
# without having to relax the rules above.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src/
!tests/

# Re-excluded because the patterns above would otherwise pull these back in.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
